1
00:00:04,370 --> 00:00:06,900
Data, a collection
of information

2
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,080
in its most basic form.

3
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:11,610
Its potential to
change the way we

4
00:00:11,610 --> 00:00:15,270
see ourselves, our
world, and our future.

5
00:00:15,270 --> 00:00:16,770
But only if it's open.

6
00:00:16,770 --> 00:00:21,300
Made available to access,
analyze, and inform action.

7
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:24,360
Open data is information
collected by government,

8
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:27,060
business, and organizations.

9
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:28,940
Added together and
made anonymous,

10
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:30,630
it's safe to be released.

11
00:00:30,630 --> 00:00:35,736
To use, reuse, and distribute.

12
00:00:35,736 --> 00:00:39,270
You already know it as things
like geospatial data, weather

13
00:00:39,270 --> 00:00:43,720
data, and government
census data.

14
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:47,190
You can use open data to
simply get from A to B.

15
00:00:47,190 --> 00:00:51,170
Or you can use open data for
more far reaching reasons,

16
00:00:51,170 --> 00:00:53,520
like making government
more transparent,

17
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:56,010
helping voters,
journalists, and politicians

18
00:00:56,010 --> 00:00:57,420
to better understand.

19
00:00:57,420 --> 00:00:59,920
And improve our society.

20
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:03,900
Open data crowdsources
expertise, pulling information

21
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:07,620
from all around the world, to
help researchers fight disease,

22
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:11,720
and relief workers
coordinate disaster response.

23
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:14,520
Open data drives
innovation helping

24
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:17,610
build new business and
more strategic investment.

25
00:01:17,610 --> 00:01:20,280
Creating new jobs,
even new industries,

26
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:22,410
and stronger economies.

27
00:01:22,410 --> 00:01:25,380
We live in an increasingly
connected world.

28
00:01:25,380 --> 00:01:27,870
Right now we've opened only
a fraction of the data that

29
00:01:27,870 --> 00:01:29,400
could benefit us.

30
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:32,670
Just as the world transformed
with the birth of the internet,

31
00:01:32,670 --> 00:01:36,060
imagine the potential
of opening up more data.

32
00:01:36,060 --> 00:01:39,240
Allowing us to see our
world from new perspectives.

33
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:43,460
Driving innovation
education and discovery.

34
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:44,690
Open data.

35
00:01:44,690 --> 00:01:46,930
Open potential.